{
 "cards": [
  {
   "dot": "cyan",
   "items": [
    "The window opens on event time and accumulates timestamped searches and clicks",
    "Either side may arrive first; the per-session buffers hold both until they meet",
    "A restart replays the input log by event time, so the rebuilt window is identical"
   ],
   "title": "Event-time accumulation"
  },
  {
   "dot": "amber",
   "items": [
    "The watermark is a threshold per upstream partition, advanced by the minimum",
    "An idle partition is parked after a timeout so it cannot hold every window hostage",
    "Parking is explicit and metered, never a silent exclusion"
   ],
   "title": "Watermark discipline"
  },
  {
   "dot": "rose",
   "items": [
    "Inside allowed lateness a laggard publishes a correction that retracts the old value",
    "Beyond the horizon it is dropped and counted, with an alert when the fraction grows",
    "The lateness budget comes from the measured lateness distribution, not a guess"
   ],
   "title": "Two late policies"
  }
 ],
